      "template": "Dear Customer,\nThank you for your question.\n\nIf your LiTime battery's state of charge (SOC) drops below 20%, the self-heating function may not activate because the battery requires sufficient charge to power the heating system. In this case, the battery will need to be \"woken up\" before it can begin charging normally.\n\nPlease try the following methods:\n\nMethod 1: Charger-First Sequence (Recommended)\n\nThis is the most reliable method for waking up the battery.\n\nDisconnect the charger from both the wall outlet and the battery.\nWait approximately 5 minutes.\nConnect the charger to the battery first (positive to positive, negative to negative).\nPlug the charger into the wall outlet.\nWait 30–60 seconds to see if charging begins.\nIf the charger still shows no activity, leave it connected for up to 30 minutes, as the BMS may require additional time to respond.\n\nMethod 2: Jump Start with a Fully Charged 12V Battery\n\nIf the first method does not work, you can use another fully charged 12V battery.\n\nConnect the good battery to the LiTime battery in parallel (positive to positive, negative to negative) using jumper cables for about 5 seconds, then disconnect it and immediately connect the LiTime charger to fully charge the battery.\n\nAlternatively:\n\nConnect the fully charged battery in parallel with the LiTime battery.\nLeave the batteries connected for 5–10 minutes.\nDisconnect the jumper cables.\nImmediately reconnect the LiTime charger using the Charger-First Sequence described above.\n\nMethod 3: Charger Pulse Activation\n\nYou can also try activating the battery by connecting the lithium charger to the battery for 5–10 seconds, disconnecting it, and repeating this process three times. This can help wake the BMS if it is in protection mode.\n\nMethod 4: Warm the Battery (Cold Weather Only)\n\nIf the battery temperature is below 32°F (0°C), the BMS will prevent charging to protect the cells.\n\nMove the battery indoors or to an environment above 50°F (10°C).\nAllow it to warm to room temperature for several hours.\nOnce warm, repeat the Charger-First Sequence.\n\nIf the battery still does not respond after trying these steps, please let us know. We'll be happy to continue troubleshooting and help get your battery operating normally.\n\nBest regards,",
